# XSH posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose() and posix_spawn_file_actions_addopen()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Effects are shown by really spawning this program as a child image (the
# test file re-runs itself with "img <mode>" arguments and reports over a
# pipe). The broad behaviour of posix_spawn() is in xsh/posix_spawn; here a
# spawn only shows what the action under test did. A descriptor number that
# is "closed" is one that was opened and closed again, which is in range.
# The functions return the error number; errno is not used.

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.001
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose() with an open descriptor returns 0.
test       t/001-close-ok.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.002
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawn.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       A child spawned with a close action for descriptor fd (open and without
           FD_CLOEXEC in the parent) has fd closed, while another open
           descriptor without an action stays open and the parent's fd
           is still open afterwards.
test       t/002-close-effect.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.003
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A close action for a descriptor that was open when the action was added
           but is already closed when the child is spawned (in range) is
           ignored: posix_spawn() returns 0, the child runs and the
           descriptor is closed in it.
test       t/003-close-ignored.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.004
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose() with a negative descriptor (-1, and
           the most negative int) returns EBADF.
test       t/004-close-ebadf.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.005
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#ERRORS
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose() with a non-negative descriptor
           number that is not open at the time of the call returns 0,
           and a spawn with that action succeeds.
test       t/005-close-notopen.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.006
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawn.html#ERRORS
class      disputed
since      2024
says       Two close actions for the same open descriptor: posix_spawn() returns 0,
           and the descriptor is closed in the child.
note       disputed (Q-89): whether a descriptor closed by an earlier action of the
           same object is "already closed at the time when the new
           process is spawned".
test       t/006-close-twice.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.007
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawn_file_actions_addopen() with a valid descriptor number, a
           pathname, flags and a mode returns 0.
test       t/007-open-ok.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.008
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawn.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       A child spawned with an open action (O_RDONLY, a descriptor number not
           open in the parent) can read from that descriptor the
           contents of the named file.
test       t/008-open-effect.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.009
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       Adding an open action with O_WRONLY|O_CREAT|O_EXCL does not create the
           file; after the spawn the file exists, with mode 0640 under a
           zero creation mask, and the child could write to the
           descriptor.
note       The run directory must not carry default ACLs (same caveat as the open()
           mode tests).
test       t/009-open-deferred.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.010
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       An open action whose descriptor is already open in the parent (the write
           end of a pipe, no FD_CLOEXEC) leaves that number, in the
           child, referring to the newly opened file (read-only, with
           its contents), not to the pipe.
test       t/010-open-replaces.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.011
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawn_file_actions_addopen() copies the pathname: overwriting the
           caller's buffer after the call and before the spawn does not
           change which file the child gets.
test       t/011-open-copies.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.012
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawn_file_actions_addopen() with a negative descriptor (-1, and
           the most negative int) returns EBADF.
test       t/012-open-ebadf-neg.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.013
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawn_file_actions_addopen() with a descriptor number equal to
           {OPEN_MAX} (and with the largest int) returns EBADF.
note       See Q-90 (the RATIONALE of addclose against the shall of addopen); the
           ERRORS text is unambiguous for addopen, so the assertion is
           required.
test       t/013-open-ebadf-max.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.014
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#ERRORS
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawn.html#ERRORS
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawn_file_actions_addopen() for a pathname that does not exist
           returns 0; a spawn with that action does not run the image:
           posix_spawn() returns an error number, or the child exits
           with status 127.
test       t/014-open-missing.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.015
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawn.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       An open action with a relative pathname and no earlier action that
           changes directory opens the file relative to the parent's
           working directory.
test       t/015-open-relative.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.016
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawn.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       With a chdir action to a directory followed by an open action for a
           relative name, the child opens the file of that name in that
           directory, not one of the same name in the parent's
           directory.
note       Needs posix_spawn_file_actions_addchdir(), new in Issue 8; a system
           without it fails to build this test.
test       t/016-open-after-chdir.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.017
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawn.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       Actions are performed in the order added: a dup2 action of descriptor a
           to b followed by a close action for a leaves b open (the same
           file) and a closed in the child.
test       t/017-order.c
